"""AI attribution: this whole file was generated by Claude (Anthropic) in Claude Code, following
design decisions made by the author. See ATTRIBUTION.md for details.

Second backbone: the freeze and the single test-set run (docs/evaluation_protocol.md, section 17), written
2026-11-25 before the test set is opened; revised the same evening after one round of independent AI review. The
first backbone's test-day code with only the backbone swapped:
  - inputs: built by the first backbone's own functions and checked against the inputs its test day stored;
  - forwards: Voxtral in VoxTurn's place (bb2_voxtral.build, bb2_pipeline.forward_states_vx), saved in the first
    backbone's test layout under data/p1v4/runs_bb2 (final/test/l1, final/test/readouts, grounding/test, offsets/test);
  - reports: p1v4_final.readout_scores, p1v4_test_report.run, p1v4_grounding_v06.main and the offsets scoring
    (bb2_report.offsets), with the run and results folders redirected (bb2_report.bind) and the second backbone's
    frozen settings; every report lists the first-backbone files it read and stops if one depends on the backbone.
Rivals do not depend on the backbone: the first backbone's test-day outputs are copied in (as on dev, bb2_report copy),
and the report checks that every rival's numbers equal the first backbone's test reports exactly.
Not run (docs/evaluation_protocol.md, section 17): the front-end noise run (G5), the package's reliance-under-noise
table that reads it, and the time-resolved ears probe on test; the reports say so instead of showing another
backbone's numbers.

Commands (repo root; PY = .venv-gpu/Scripts/python.exe -X utf8):
  laptop  rehearse              dev rehearsal of the report path: this backbone's dev outputs laid out as a final run
                                (runs_bb2/final/dev), read-out scores, decision table, grounding report with its natural
                                part and the G5 stub branch -> results/main_v04_bb2/*_dev_rehearsal.json
  GPU     forward dev <n>       smoke run of the GPU path on the first n dev items of every set (outputs under
                                runs_bb2/smoke_dev), then `smoke-check`: equal to the stored dev outputs
  laptop  freeze make|check     results/main_v04_bb2/freeze_bb2.json: sha256 of checkpoint, base model, read-outs,
                                settings, dev results, code (module closure) and plan; written once, on a clean tree
  laptop  freeze amend <file ...> --reason <text>   after a bug fix: re-hash only the named, recorded files
  laptop  items                 P1V4_FINAL_RUN=1 (both records checked): examples_test.json and items/test*.json
  laptop  freeze athena         the hash list that the GPU job checks first: the record's checkpoint, base model
                                and code, plus the hashes of the test inputs uploaded after the freeze
  GPU     forward test          old-head scoring pass on natural test (= p1v4_final
                                run_l1), then testnat (batch 8), testgrd (batch 1), testoff (batch 1)
  laptop  copy                  P1V4_FINAL_RUN=1: the first backbone's backbone-independent test outputs into runs_bb2
  laptop  readouts              P1V4_FINAL_RUN=1: every read-out's scores on natural test (p1v4_final.readout_scores)
  laptop  report                P1V4_FINAL_RUN=1: offsets (G4b), decision table, grounding package v0.6 on test
Known differences besides the backbone: row 5's practical advantage uses the first backbone's laptop latency file
(not measured here); the offsets are scored from float16 features (as this backbone's dev offsets).
"""
